<div class="legal-content">
  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>ISS Tracker (also listed as Space Station Tracker) is provided by Restart. This policy applies to the Android and iOS apps. The app does not require an account. If you contact support, we receive the email address, message, and any information you choose to include so we can respond.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Location</h2>
    <p>ISS Tracker requests location permission to find visible ISS passes and configure pass alerts. Predictions are calculated on your device using downloaded orbital elements; the app does not send your coordinates to CelesTrak or Where the ISS at? to calculate passes. The platform location service and reverse-geocoding service may process your coordinates to determine your position and a nearby place name, under the platform provider's privacy terms. Saved alert coordinates, altitude, and place names are stored locally. ISS Tracker does not operate a server that stores your location history.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Local App Data</h2>
    <p>Your theme, map preferences, alert configuration, scheduled reminder information, purchase entitlement flag, review eligibility, advertising launch count, and cached orbital elements are stored using platform storage. These settings are not synced through an ISS Tracker account. Device backups or device-to-device transfers may retain or restore local data according to your operating-system settings.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Notifications and Calendar</h2>
    <p>Reminders are scheduled as local device notifications. Automatic alerts may use background refresh and, on Android, alarm scheduling. Calendar access or the system calendar editor is used when you choose to add a pass. Calendar entries and content you explicitly share are handled by the destination app or service. You can revoke permissions in system settings. Disabling automatic alerts does not cancel manually scheduled reminders or delete calendar entries.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Advertising and Consent</h2>
    <p>ISS Tracker uses Google AdMob and Google User Messaging Platform. Advertising requests begin only when Google's consent status says ads may be requested. Depending on your region and choices, Google and its partners may process device information, IP address, advertising identifiers, approximate location, and ad interactions to deliver and measure ads.</p>
    <p>On iOS, the app requests App Tracking Transparency permission when applicable before preparing advertising consent. The app remains usable if you decline tracking. A Privacy Choices entry is shown when Google requires one. AdMob choices and Apple's tracking permission do not themselves disable the app's separately enabled Analytics or Crashlytics collection.</p>
    <p>Google's privacy policy is available at <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">https://policies.google.com/privacy</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Purchases</h2>
    <p>The optional lifetime ad-removal purchase is processed by Google Play or the Apple App Store. The app uses store purchase records and entitlement status to complete and restore the purchase and stores an ad-removal flag locally. ISS Tracker does not receive your payment-card details. Removing ads does not disable Analytics, Crashlytics, maps, or other network requests.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Analytics and Diagnostics</h2>
    <p>ISS Tracker uses Google Analytics for Firebase to measure app launches, sessions, active users, screen views, feature interactions, settings changes, and purchase-flow outcomes. This helps understand general usage and improve the app. ISS Tracker does not send precise coordinates, saved location names, astronaut names, live-stream URLs, calendar or notification contents, support-email contents, payment-card details, transaction identifiers, or raw diagnostic messages as custom analytics parameters. The Analytics SDK uses an app-instance identifier and may derive approximate location and device information as described by Google. Advertising personalization signals from Analytics are disabled by default.</p>
    <p>ISS Tracker also includes Firebase Crashlytics on Android and iOS. Crashlytics automatically collects crash reports and related diagnostics, including installation identifiers, stack traces, exception information, app version, and device/operating-system information, to help investigate failures. Analytics events may also appear as crash-report breadcrumbs.</p>
    <p>Analytics and Crashlytics are currently enabled separately from advertising consent, and the app does not currently provide an in-app switch for either service. Google's descriptions of these services and their data handling are available at <a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy">https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">https://policies.google.com/privacy</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Third-Party Data Providers</h2>
    <p>The app downloads satellite positions and orbital elements from Where the ISS at? and CelesTrak, crew information and live-stream listings from GitHub-hosted feeds, and biographies and images from Wikipedia/Wikimedia and other image hosts referenced by those feeds. Maps use Google Maps on Android and Apple MapKit on iOS. Opening a live stream or another external link sends you to YouTube or the selected destination service. Requests expose standard network information such as your IP address to the relevant provider; map requests also identify the area being displayed. Each provider applies its own privacy terms. Apple describes its practices at <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/</a> and GitHub at <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Retention, Deletion, and Security</h2>
    <p>Local settings and saved alert locations are retained until app data is cleared or the app is deleted, subject to platform backup and restore behavior. On iOS, offloading an app can retain its data. Pending notifications and calendar entries are managed by the operating system; delete calendar entries separately in your calendar app.</p>
    <p>Uninstalling the app does not delete information already received by Google or other providers, store purchase records, backups, or support emails. Analytics retention depends on the project's Google Analytics settings and the type of data. Firebase currently states that Crashlytics retains crash traces and associated identifiers for 90 days before beginning removal from live and backup systems. Providers may retain other records under their own policies or legal obligations. Support correspondence is retained as needed to address the request and meet applicable obligations. Contact <a href="mailto:restartapplication@gmail.com">restartapplication@gmail.com</a> to ask about access or deletion; we will explain what records we can identify and what requests must be handled by the relevant provider.</p>
    <p>App data requests use HTTPS, and providers may process information in other countries. Device storage and backups are protected by platform controls. No network or storage system can be guaranteed completely secure.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>ISS Tracker is not directed to children under 13. If you believe a child has provided personal information through the app or support, contact us so we can investigate and address it. The app has no user accounts; this does not mean its third-party SDKs collect no data.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Your Choices</h2>
    <p>You can change location, notification, tracking, and advertising choices where the platform or consent form offers them, and clear local app data through platform controls. Access, correction, deletion, objection, or other privacy rights may apply depending on where you live. Contact us to exercise applicable rights or ask about the current retention settings. You may also contact your relevant data-protection authority.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Changes and Contact</h2>
    <p>This policy may be updated when app features or third-party services change. The date above identifies the latest revision. Questions can be sent to Restart at <a href="mailto:restartapplication@gmail.com">restartapplication@gmail.com</a>.</p>
  </section>
</div>
